# sn0wbite T8006 adaptation of the qemu-t8030 fork.
# Apply on a clean qemu-t8030 checkout:  cd qemu-t8030 && git apply <this>  then build
# (see docs/watchos/qemu-build-and-boot.md). Run with -smp 2 (the S5's two cores).
# Covers:
#  (1) apple_a13.c: CPU node made optional for single-cluster Tempest (S5);
#  (2) sn0w CPU compat layer (hw/arm/sn0w_cpu.{c,h}) + hook -> RAZ/WI the Apple IMPDEF
#      (op0=3,CRn=15) sysreg space (canonical source in tools/opwwe231/watchos/qemu/sn0w/);
#  (3) t8030.c: minimal boot-to-console machine (coprocessor creates skipped, nvram optional),
#      timebase-frequency provided on the DT root + cpu nodes (24 MHz);
#  (4) xnu.c KEEP_COMP: whitelist apple,tempest so the DT filter keeps the S5 /cpus nodes.
#
